<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77779" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρα-βάτης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[βᾰ]</span>, poet. and early 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραιβάτης</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12.5
		</span></i>, etc.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραβαίνω</span> I) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who stands beside</i>: prop.
				<i>the warrior</i> or <i>combatant who stands beside the
				charioteer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἂν δ᾽ ἔβαν ἐν δίφροισι παραιβάται
					ἡνίοχοί τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.132
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραιβάτας ἔστησαν ἐς τάξιν δορός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					677
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναλαβεῖν τοὺς παραβάτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					7.1.29
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύο δ᾽ εἰσὶν ἐπὶ τῷ ἅρματι π. πρὸς
					ἡνιόχῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					15.1.52
				</span></i>
			: =
			
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποβάται</span>, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				7.73
			</span></i>; fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραιβάτις</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.754
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> light troops
				(<i>velites</i>) who <i>ran beside</i> the cavalry, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Aem.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραβαίνω</span> II. <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>) <i>transgressor</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				553
			</span></i> (lyr., in poet. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρβάτης</span></b> ), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Sm.
				<u>Ps.</u>
				16(17).4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. θεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Polem.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Macr.
				<u>Sat.</u>
				5.19.29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. νόμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
					2.25
				</span></i>
			.</div>
